class_name PlaceholderArt
extends RefCounted

## The road for art that has not arrived yet (task 0120).
##
## From phase 10 on, code tasks put new things on screen long before Codex has
## drawn them. Each such thing is drawn through **a stand-in at the real pack's
## canvas and pivot**, found through the same lookup the views use for real
## art - so the day the pack is integrated, its leaf deletes the entry here and
## no view code changes.
##
## ## The lookup
##
## `frame(path)` is the one place `src/ui/` reads raster geometry: it answers
## from `RasterArt.FRAMES` (generated by `tools/import_art.py`) first and from
## this registry second. `texture_path(path)` says which file to load for a
## path - the path itself once it is raster art, the stand-in's file before.
## `_task_0120_placeholders` in `headless_v1` fails on any other file in
## `src/ui/` reading `RasterArt.FRAMES` directly.
##
## The farmer has a second door, because his animations are named rather than
## pathed: `PlayerArt.animation(name)` answers from `PlayerFrames` first and
## from `POSES` here second, and `PlayerArt.texture_path(name, frame)` returns
## the stand-in's frame for a registered name.
##
## ## Adding an entry
##
## One line in `POSES` per runtime animation the code draws before its pack is
## integrated: the pack id, the frames, seconds and loop from the pack's
## Deliverables table (`implementation/backlog/packs/Axxx-*.md`), the stand-in
## it plays meanwhile, the stand-in's own geometry and the pack's final one,
## and `"spec_after"` when the pack waits on a game task for its geometry.
## A stand-in is **never a hand-painted PNG**: an existing texture (reused,
## tinted, scaled or mirrored), an ASCII map in `tools/sprite_maps.py` built by
## `tools/gen_sprites.py` and owned `ascii` in
## `assets/art_source/ownership.json`, or a code-drawn shape - drawn at the
## canvas and pivot the real art will have, so placement and y-sorting do not
## move when it arrives. **Keep each entry on one line**: `tools/placeholders.py`
## reads them line by line.
##
## Art that is not the farmer's - A003's guardian, A004's cursor (task 0131) -
## goes in `ART` instead, with the folder its pack delivers to; an empty
## `stand_in` there means the view draws it in code (`is_drawn`).
##
## ## Deleting an entry
##
## When the pack's raster outputs land at the runtime paths, the leaf that
## integrates it deletes its lines here; `python tools/placeholders.py --check`
## (run by verify) fails while an entry names a pack already `integrated` or a
## path that is already raster-owned.

const DIR := "res://sprites/actors/"

